PART 8 — GLASSMORPHISM SYSTEM
========================================================

Glassmorphism must be restrained and purposeful.

Create three surface categories.

LEVEL 1 — SOLID SURFACES

For:

- Main page backgrounds.
- Long text.
- Content-heavy sections.
- Dashboard content.
- Message history.

Use solid or nearly solid surfaces.

LEVEL 2 — SUBTLE GLASS

For:

- Public navigation.
- Floating navigation elements.
- Selected preview panels.
- Contextual panels.
- Selected overlays.

Use controlled transparency and subtle backdrop blur.

LEVEL 3 — FLOATING GLASS

For:

- Dropdown menus.
- Popovers.
- Command palette.
- Dialogs.
- Floating toolbars.

Use slightly stronger separation and shadows.

Create reusable variables:

--nx-glass-bg
--nx-glass-border
--nx-glass-blur
--nx-glass-shadow

Do not apply glass effects to every card.

Avoid nested backdrop-filter effects.

Ensure text remains readable in both themes.

